# The routes to the glyph raster, and how each meets the clipping
# region. Held by tests/check-show-clip.sh, which derives every line
# from the sources rather than reading them: a line here is a record of
# what the tree holds, and a route that arrives or leaves shows up as a
# line to write or retire.
#
# reads-cache      a C binding that reaches the raster with the region
#                  taken out of the clip's cache holder. Every route a
#                  program has to it must run .showclip first, and the
#                  check holds them to that.
# narrows-itself   a C binding that reaches the raster and narrows it by
#                  means of its own, so its callers are not held to
#                  .showclip. Each line is a claim about a binding, and
#                  the claim is why the line is here rather than under
#                  reads-cache.
# resolves         a language operator whose body runs .showclip before
#                  it reaches the raster.
#
# .maskcachehit replays a stored glyph mask only where the clip is a
# rectangle that holds the whole raster, and refuses otherwise, so a
# glyph the region's edge crosses is built again and painted through the
# ordinary fill. .stencilaa paints a small stencil mask for the image
# machinery, which has met the region in the fill that called it.

entries 13

reads-cache show
reads-cache ashow
reads-cache widthshow
reads-cache awidthshow
reads-cache .glyphshow
reads-cache .glyphshowidx

narrows-itself .maskcachehit
narrows-itself .stencilaa

resolves show
resolves ashow
resolves widthshow
resolves awidthshow
resolves glyphshow
